// Codex 7: Clippy's instructions. The private-to-Clippy channel: each
// entry is unlocked for the CHARACTER Clippy only (main.loom rules:
// `unlock Clippy Instructions N for Clippy`), so it lands in her booth's
// Codex (the Codex tile on her Mission) the moment the cue fires. Instructions 1 is
// held from the start. Never `about: Clippy` (that would put the
// instructions on her People card for every guest to read).
//
// CI 1, CI 2 and the top of CI 3 follow the Oct 30 script. Her words are the
// story's beats and reach her teleprompter; what is here is everything a beat
// can't carry, because a line in a beat reaches every phone: the script's stage
// directions, word for word, and the phone steps, marked (App).
// core/test/trapped-w58-script.test.ts compares them. CI 3's rest and CI 4 to
// CI 9 are INVENTED for the rewrite (the source has only a copy-pasted "3/X"
// title) and are flagged for review (design spec §10.1).
//
// Nothing here may mention Sandy, the server room or the patch bay: a
// performer's codex rides along when she talks to Trabolta.

// Wave 58: rewritten from the Oct 30 script.
// DRAFT w58 (the (App) lines and the wording round the script's directions)
CODEX Clippy Instructions 1
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 1/X - BEGINNING OF NIGHT
  category: Missions
  known to: Clippy
  text:
    - (App) A host starts Computer Bingo: your words pop up on your
    teleprompter. Read them out loud, then ✓ Done. They are the script: every
    host's name, the prize, the rules. The hosts have no lines of their own.
    - At "First, let's meet your hosts!": Gesture to each host.
    - At "Our first activity is Computer Bingo!": Hand out bingo cards and
    markers.
    - Then send them off. The clock is already running: 20 minutes.

// w21 (reverses w18's B6): the hosts and the directors call every cue; Clippy runs the games in the room and plays for ⭐ Points.
// w26 (B1, B2, B5): a guest may call BINGO from their phone; ↩ Not a Bingo; one round.
// Wave 58: rewritten from the Oct 30 script; 🤐 no longer ends with nobody going.
// DRAFT w58 (the (App) lines and the wording round the script's directions)
CODEX Clippy Instructions 2
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 2/X - COMPUTER BINGO RESULTS
  category: Missions
  text:
    - (App) A host calls ⏰: your first words pop up on your teleprompter.
    Every press below brings up the next words. Read them, then ✓ Done: PLAYER
    SELECT is under the teleprompter until you do.
    - Invite each winner forward, one at a time.
    - (App) Press 🎱 Bingo winner on each winner's card: "Let's hear your
    winning line." Several winners are fine. A program may call BINGO from
    their own phone: your words for their line come straight up, and their
    card pops up for you. If their line holds, 🎱 on them; if it doesn't, ↩ Not
    a Bingo, and Bingo picks up with the time it had left. There is only one
    round: the first 🎯 or 🤐 ends it, so the others never come up.
    - Let the winner read their matches. When they reach the centre square,
    go on to "And for our centre square".
    - Wait for an answer. Make sure they clearly identify the program.
    - Prepare to present the winner's Bingo Floppy Disk.
    - (App) Press 🎀 Award a ribbon on the winner's card, then 🎯 on the
    program they named. The winner may even name themselves: 🎯 on their own
    card.
    - The Antivirus interrupts and announces that the identified program
    needs to be reinstalled. Stop and let them explain. Remain cheerful and
    attentive.
    - If the winner refuses to identify their match: (App) 🤐 on the winner,
    and your line pops up. If they still refuse, let the Antivirus decide who
    needs reinstallation. Follow their direction.
    - If nobody completed a Bingo, (App) Task Manager presses 🃏 on the
    designated anti-AI program (MS Paint, unless the director changed it),
    and your words pop up: Task Manager supplies a card marked as a completed
    Bingo. Read the name provided.
    - If the program denies completing the card, pause and let the Antivirus
    respond. Otherwise, proceed through the winning line, saving the centre
    square for last. (App) 🎱 on them.
    - (App) If they deny the card, 🎯 on them first: that marks them, and Norton
    interrupts.
    - (App) Norton presses 🛡 Send to the Internet on the program going to
    the Internet. You do not press it. As the selected program is escorted to
    the Internet, your reassurance pops up.
    - (App) If a program is walking, a host presses 📺: the reinstallation
    appears on the screen and your words pop up. If not, nothing happens: go
    straight on.
    - Draw everyone's attention to the screen.
    - Continue to respond with cheerful encouragement. Treat the process as
    routine, even if the other guests seem uncomfortable.
    - (App) A host presses 🎤: your words about Jean Trabolta pop up. They end
    "Trabolta, would you explain the rules?": a host presses 🤖 on that. He
    comes online and speaks on the TV: his speech, the three questions, his
    sign-off, about three minutes. Let him finish.
    - (App) Then talk with him, out loud, in front of everyone. Task Manager
    types what you say and he answers on the TV. Banter: welcome him, ask
    about the shop, tease him a little, but never about the accident. A
    minute or so, then a host starts 🔎.

// w21 (reverses w18's B6): the hosts and the directors call every cue; Clippy runs the games in the room and plays for ⭐ Points.
// w18b (Q6, R20, R21): Trabolta reads the results on the TV; the
// bottle comes after the third; "confident answers are accepted" is gone.
// w26 (G1: never say the rules out loud; D1: a Dare makes a scene)
// DRAFT w32 (the talk scene between the spins)
// DRAFT w58 (the top: Part 3 of the Oct 30 script, split around the window)
CODEX Clippy Instructions 3
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 3/X - FIRST MOMENT OF TRUTH
  category: Missions
  text:
    - (App) A host presses ⚖️: your welcome back pops up on your teleprompter.
    Read it, then ✓ Done. Two minutes of last-chance filing start with it: the
    phones and the TV carry the window, so never say it out loud.
    - Never say the rules out loud: let the room learn them from the results.
    (For you alone: an accurate answer is accepted; one filed one hundred
    percent sure is accepted even if it is nonsensical; an inaccurate answer
    filed with normal or low confidence, or a clear guess, is a symptom of
    corruption.)
    - (App) A host closes the window with ⏱ (or it closes itself at two
    minutes), and your hand-over to Trabolta pops up. A closed round never
    reopens.
    - (App) A host fires 📋 Results for each question in turn: nod to
    them when the room is ready. Trabolta reads the result on the TV: CONSENSUS (every answer
    matches and everyone was sure), nobody filed, or the list of what
    everyone told him, with how many were accepted and how many were
    guesses. When he has finished, the next 📋. Then say that guesses are
    a symptom of corruption. The app settles the filings on its own:
    +50 Truthcoin for an accepted answer, a mark for a guess.
    - Never say which filings were lies: the room hears "accepted" for
    every confident answer.
    - After question three, Truth or Dare: when he has finished the third,
    a host spins 🍾 the bottle, about five spins (NEXT offers five; spin
    more if the room wants it). The bottle's program pops up on your phone. Trabolta names the program on the TV;
    their phone asks Truth or Dare.
    - Dare: they are marked for reinstallation for not choosing Truth, and
    Trabolta makes a scene on the TV: he orders the Antivirus to take them
    to the Internet. (App) If their phone is dead, 🎩 Chose Dare on their
    card does the same.
    - Truth: Trabolta asks them a personal question on the TV. Make them
    answer it, in front of everyone. (App) 🗣 Truth answered on their card
    when they do; 🙅 Truth refused if they will not — a refusal is marked
    for reinstallation and escorted.
    - Between the spins, talk with Trabolta out loud (Task Manager types
    what you say): he is starving for truth and every guess stings him.
    Needle him a little. Dare him to pick truth or dare himself.
    - After the spins, the second hunt is previewed (📺).
    - Ribbons are always allowed: 🎀 Award a ribbon on anyone who deserves
    one.

// w21 (reverses w18's B6): the hosts and the directors call every cue; Clippy runs the games in the room and plays for ⭐ Points.
// DRAFT w32 (the talk scene at the ad attack)
CODEX Clippy Instructions 4
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 4/X - THE MALWARE
  category: Missions
  text:
    - Begin previewing the second round of the Truth Scavenger Hunt. The
    presentation will be hijacked by an advertisement nobody understands.
    - Then this message from Trabolta arrives on your phone. It is for
    you only. "Don't let everyone know but if the malware continues we
    are all going to die. Tell them something reassuring. I know this is
    probably creating some intense emotions for you but try not to show
    the others."
    - Everyone else receives a slightly different message that downplays
    the situation.
    - Overreact wildly. Become apoplectic with fear: this is the one thing
    you never want to see happen in your computer.
    - Trabolta speaks through the advertisement, and it hurts him. Talk
    with him, out loud (Task Manager types what you say): ask what is
    happening, whether he is hurt, who did this. Panic with him, then
    pull yourself together. More adverts may burst through while you
    talk.
    - Then convey: "There are signs of malware in the system that we need
    to be very vigilant about. We are going to proceed on the Truth
    Scavenger Hunt because it is more important than ever that Trabolta
    gets the information he needs to undo what is happening."
    - (App) A host fires 📓 Hunt 2. The questions go up on the screen
    and into everyone's Quest Log.
    - Disperse everyone for one hour, with instructions to return for the
    Second Moment of Truth.

// w21 (reverses w18's B6): the hosts and the directors call every cue; Clippy runs the games in the room and plays for ⭐ Points.
CODEX Clippy Instructions 5
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 5/X - TRUTH PONG
  category: Missions
  text:
    - Everyone has just been told they have five minutes to reach the
    Desktop. Anyone late without Bathroom Mode is taken to the Internet
    by an Antivirus, and does not get to play Truth Pong.
    - When everyone is assembled, be visibly distraught. Behind the tears,
    try to act more excited than ever: "It's Truth Time again! This time
    we are going to reveal truths in a fun new way, with a game of Truth
    Pong. Everyone's favourite game!"
    - The rules: there is a beer-cup pyramid on a folding table outside.
    We are all going to show that we are functional programs who are
    trusted to retrieve truths accurately, by following a simple command:
    bounce or throw a ping-pong ball into a cup. We should all be able to
    do this, because we are being commanded.
    - Miss the cup: you are not trusted to deliver a truth, and you need
    to be reinstalled in the Internet. (App) 🏓 Missed the cup.
    - Make the cup: you may share one truth, and answer one of the facts
    Trabolta asked for. (App) 🏓 Made the cup.
    - Same judging as before, only for programs who made the cup: ✅ or 😤
    for the question they answered (🔢 picks the question: 1 to start), or
    🤷 to the Internet.
    - When a host fires the tally, Trabolta welcomes everyone back. He
    reads this round's answers later, after the beans.

// DRAFT w32 (the talk scene at the beans)
CODEX Clippy Instructions 6
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 6/X - THE TRUST CHART AND THE BEANS
  category: Missions
  text:
    - Trabolta presents his Trust Chart and ranks everyone. When he names
    the most trusted program, lead the applause. Applaud like your life
    depends on it.
    - When he berates the least trusted program, do not defend them.
    - Trabolta will order VLC to print a certificate for the hero. When
    the printer fails, MS Paint may encourage VLC to open it up. Let it
    happen.
    - The printer is full of beans. Clock it immediately as the malware
    getting worse: "Routine operations like print to PDF are no longer
    working. It is even more urgent that we get the next facts right."
    - Trabolta is coming apart. Talk with him, out loud (Task Manager
    types what you say): comfort him, and pry a little. He says things he
    takes back at once. Never repeat them for him.
    - Trabolta then orders the Antivirus to zip everyone out of the
    Internet. Encourage everyone to welcome the zipped programs back.
    They are compressed for the moment. Do not open them.

CODEX Clippy Instructions 7
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 7/X - MIDNIGHT
  category: Missions
  text:
    - The system clock has reset to 11 PM, December 31, 1999. Trabolta
    explains what happens at midnight: best case, the clocks go back to
    January 1, 1900, and we wait 94 years for Internet in Halifax. Worst
    case, the Y2K Bug.
    - This is the final round. The final facts are in everyone's Quest
    Log, and the clock counts down to midnight on everyone's phone.
    - Some programs will start recruiting others to their side. You may
    not take sides on air. You are Clippy: you are here for everyone.
    - Keep everyone hunting for the final facts. At midnight, everyone is
    called back to the Desktop for the final reveal.

// w21 (reverses w18's B6): the hosts and the directors call every cue; Clippy runs the games in the room and plays for ⭐ Points.
CODEX Clippy Instructions 8
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 8/X - THE FINAL REVEAL
  category: Missions
  text:
    - The lights go dark. Let everyone know it is time for anyone who has
    found the final facts to speak up.
    - Everyone may speak: what they have learned, what facts they have
    gathered, what they believe but cannot prove, and what they think
    SHOULD happen next.
    - (App) Judge the final facts as before: ✅ or 😤 for question 1, 2 or 3
    (🔢 picks it), or 🤷 to the Internet.
    - Acknowledge every contribution. Then: "There is only one version of
    the truth. Because truth is always in binary."
    - Trabolta then reads all three final answers, the trust leaderboard and
    the winner on the TV, and hands back to you.
    - (App) A host fires 🍎 Bobbing for Truth: your phone says your game is on.
    - Dejectedly introduce the final Truth Game of the night: "Trabolta has
    prepared a summary of his findings so far, but we are not worthy of
    the truth unless we are willing to Bob for it and risk our status as
    a program."
    - Nothing proceeds until someone successfully bobs and brings up the
    Bag of Truth. (App) 🍎 Brought up the Bag of Truth on the winner. A
    program who comes up empty: 🍎 Failed the bob, to the Internet.
    - Before the bag can be read, Trabolta stops everyone to deliver his
    assessment of everyone's trustworthiness. Let him.
    - Then the program who brought up the bag reads truth.txt aloud, when
    a host fires it.

CODEX Clippy Instructions 9
  title: CLIPPY INSTRUCTIONS - 9/X - PURGATORY
  category: Missions
  text:
    - The computer has been turned off. The lights go out, every phone
    says GO TO THE DESKTOP, and the dance song plays. Dance.
    - (App) After the song, the director fires "Clippy reads the summary".
    The summary pops up on your phone, on the teleprompter.
    - Read the summary aloud. It ends on the verdict below.
    - Deliver the verdict: "Because of our actions, the computer was
    turned off without Shut Down properly being followed, and all of our
    progress has been erased. Our corporeal forms are in the Optical
    Drive, and they have all passed away. We are now in
    purgatory forever together, which is pretty similar to being stuck in
    a computer."
